<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43254" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑτέρ-ωσε</span></b> , Adv.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to the other side</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				4.492
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				16.179
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔνθεν μὲν . . , ἑ. δὲ . .</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Sph.</u>
					224a
				</span></i>
			; <i>on one side</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑ. κάρη βάλεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					8.306
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				22.17
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> in pregnant
			sense with certain Verbs, <i>on the other side</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ δ᾽ ἑ. καθῖζον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					20.151
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κἂν ἑ. πατάξῃ τις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					4.40
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄλλοσε</span>
			, <i>elsewhither, aside</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑ. λιασθείς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					23.231
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κύνες ἑ. φόβηθεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					16.163
				</span></i>
			, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑ. τρέχων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Ach.</u>
					828
				</span></i>
			; also 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς ἑ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					4.1315
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>elsewhere</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Charid.</u>
				22
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
